{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "route": {
    "route_id": "eastern-railway",
    "name": "Eastern Railway (Afula-Tulkarm-Lydda)",
    "name_arabic": "السكة الشرقية",
    "countries": "Israel, Palestine",
    "gauge_mm": 1050,
    "year_opened": 1915,
    "era": "historic",
    "color": "#b45309",
    "corridor_confidence": "medium",
    "description": "WWI Ottoman/German line; later standard-gauged",
    "notes": "Engineered by Heinrich Meissner under Ottoman direction — the same engineer as the Hejaz Railway.  [gauge_mm] Built as 1,050 mm NARROW gauge (Ottoman/German, WWI); CONVERTED to standard gauge (1,435 mm) by the British EEF in 1917-18. The project’s '1050/1435' captures both eras.  [route] A BRANCHING network, not a single line: the through spine ran Afula -> Jenin -> Mas’udiya -> Tulkarm -> Lydda, with a spur SE to NABLUS (from Mas’udiya; the 1908-1914 Afula-Nablus branch) and a branch NW to HADERA on the coast (from Tulkarm). Nablus and Hadera are held as off-line extra_stations. The project’s 'Hadera-Tulkarm-Lydda' describes the coastal-plain portion of this network.  [historic_vs_modern] NAME CLASH: a MODERN 'Eastern Railway' (Israel Railways, Rosh HaAyin-Kfar Saba-Hadera, opened from 2016) revives the name and roughly the coastal-plain corridor, but it is a NEW standard-gauge line — distinct from this historic WWI Ottoman/German railway.",
    "history": "A WWI-era line built under Ottoman direction by the German engineer Heinrich Meissner. A branch from Afula (on the Jezreel Valley line) toward Jerusalem was begun in 1908 and reached Nablus by 1914; from 1915 Meissner built a 1,050 mm line west from El Mas'udiya to Tulkarm, with branches north to Hadera and south to Lydda (linking the Jaffa-Jerusalem line). Intermediate halts + Nablus-branch junction stations added from the 1925 PR Diagram. Chainage from Afula; values beyond Mas'udiya derived by joining the map's Nablus-branch chaining at the shared Mas'udiya junction. Qalqilya/Lydda chainage left null (not on this sheet's eastern chaining). Segment geometry reset to schematic on re-sequencing.",
    "verification_status": "unverified",
    "source_ids": [
      "levantrain_compilation",
      "levantrain_system",
      "os_near_east_railways_1919",
      "pr_diagram_1925",
      "wp_israel_rw",
      "wp_palestine_rw"
    ]
  },
